node_modules
.output
.nitro
.tanstack
dist
# Every shape of it: `.env`, `.env.local`, and any one-off copy made while debugging
# (`.env.backup-before-pooler` was a real one: a full copy of production credentials that
# sat untracked and unignored for two days because the old rule only matched the literal
# name). The template is the one exception; it holds no secret, only variable names.
.env*
!.env.example
# Baileys credentials: linking a WhatsApp number writes real session keys here.
.wa-auth
# Uploaded knowledge-base files held on disk before ingest.
uploads

# Google Drive's sync scratch directories. They appear in the repo root because the folder
# is synced, have nothing to do with the project, and would otherwise be committed by anyone
# running `git add -A`. Both directions, only the upload half was listed here for a while,
# which is the same oversight as the `.env*` note above in a less expensive place.
.tmp.driveupload
.tmp.drivedownload

# Local TLS material. Nothing in this repo reads it, and an empty directory is not the state
# to write rules for: the one that matters is the day somebody drops a private key in here
# and the next `git add -A` commits it.
certs
